**Redundancy:
--> Redundancy means how many copies of your data azure keeps and where they are stored.
1. LRS: Locally Redundant Storage
--> Azure keeps 3 copies of your data.
--> all in one data center
--> cheapest option
--> if data center fails --> data loss

2. ZRS: Zone-Redundant Storage
--> data stores in 3 zones within 1region
--> each zone --> 1 copy
--> survives zone failure
--> reliable than LRS

3. GRS: Geo Redundant Sorage
--> azure keeps total 6 copies of your data.
--> azure store 3 copies locally + 3 copies in another region
--> you can not access the secondary unless failover is done
--> useful for disaster recovery

4. GZRS: Geo-Zone Redundant Storage
--> Combines ZRS + GRS
--> keeeps total 6 copies of your data.
--> stored 3 copies in primary region (ZRS) + 3 copies in another region (ZRS)

